{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} CONFIG FILE READ ERROR - using default}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 2_2X3X6}
\pard \b CONFIG FILE READ ERROR - using default 
\par \plain\fs24 This error is given when a file error is detected on reading the configuration file CONFIG.LEO 
\par or when a format error is detected.
\par This file contains the configuration data (options etc) for the Right Hand Side of the SEM (electronics).
\par When this error occurs a default minimum configuration is assumed.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} CONFIG FILE WRITE ERROR}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 1KL.SH}
\pard \b CONFIG FILE WRITE ERROR 
\par \plain\fs24 This error is given when a file error is detected on writing the configuration file CONFIG.LEO.
\par 
\par This file contains the configuration data (options etc) for the Right Hand Side of the SEM (electronics).
\par The most likely cause of error is inadequate disk space.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Cannot print colour TIFF}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 18XJ6YQ}
\pard \b Cannot print colour TIFF
\par 
\par \plain\fs24 This error is given when an attempt is made to print a TIFF file which contains a real colour image.
\par 
\par The printer can only print Grey or binary files.
\par 
\par \page
