{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} DEFAULT.VAC FILE USED}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 153IGVQ}
\pard \b DEFAULT.VAC FILE USED
\par \plain\fs24 Configuration and calibration information relating to the column is saved in Non Volatile RAM. 
\par Due to a problem reading the NVRAM an attempt has been made to use the standby DATA.VAC file and either the data is corrupt, an incompatible version or the file could not be found. The file DEFAULT.VAC has been used which contains a default set of data. Any calibration data has therefore been lost.
\par 
\par \uldb \f3\fs20 Report problem\plain\f3\fs20 {\v P8W0Q0}\f1\fs24 
\par 
\par \page
