{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Vacuum Command error}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} 1WGWYTQ}
\pard \b Vacuum Command error
\par 
\par \plain\fs24 This error is given when a vacuum command fails.
\par 
\par Code numbers greater than 40 indicate the failure of an internal consistency check.  \ul \f3\ul\fs20 Contact LEO\plain\f3\fs20 {\v 2JJ8T6_}\f1\fs24 
\par 
\par Code numbers  less than 40 indicate that there is a failure in the communication to the stage/vac subsystem.
\par \uldb \f3\fs20 Report problem\plain\f3\fs20 {\v P8W0Q0}\f1\fs24 
\par 
\par The code number given identifies the failing command as follows:
\par 
\par  1  CONFIGURE_FRONT_PANEL_REQ 
\par  2 SYSTEM_PUMPING_REQ                       
\par \pard  3 CONFIG_VIEWING_WINDOW_REQ     
\par  4 CONFIG_COLUMN_PUMPING_REQ     
\par  5 COLUMN_PUMPING_REQ                     
\par  6 COLUMN_ISOLN_REPLY_REQ              
\par  7 EDX_CONFIGURE_REQ                         
\par  8 WDX_CONFIGURE_REQ                        
