{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Stage Limits}
\pard \b Stage Limits
\par 
\par \plain\fs24 The motorised stage has six limits per axis:
\par \f3\fs20 
\par \pard\li425 \f1\fs24 Low Outer
\par Low Inner
\par Low User
\par 
\par \pard Normal working range
\par 
\par \pard\li425 High User
\par High Inner
\par High Outer
\par \pard .
\par The user limits are defined by the user, by default they are set at the outer limits.
\par 
\par If an inner limit is detected the stage slows down and does not lose position.
\par If an outer limit is detected the stage stops immediately and position is lost.
\par Note that an outer limit should not be detected except in hardware error conditions (e.g. dirty track/contact on stage limit PCB failing to detect inner limit).
\par 
\par 
