{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Vacuum Command error}
\pard \b Vacuum Command error
\par 
\par \plain\fs24 This error is given when a vacuum command fails.
\par 
\par Code numbers greater than 40 indicate the failure of an internal consistency check.  \ul \f3\ul\fs20 Contact LEO\plain\f3\fs20 {\v 2JJ8T6_}\f1\fs24 
\par 
\par Code numbers  less than 40 indicate that there is a failure in the communication to the stage/vac subsystem.
\par \uldb \f3\fs20 Report problem\plain\f3\fs20 {\v P8W0Q0}\f1\fs24 
\par 
\par The code number given identifies the failing command as follows:
\par 
\par  1  CONFIGURE_FRONT_PANEL_REQ 
\par  2 SYSTEM_PUMPING_REQ                       
\par \pard  3 CONFIG_VIEWING_WINDOW_REQ     
\par  4 CONFIG_COLUMN_PUMPING_REQ     
\par  5 COLUMN_PUMPING_REQ                     
\par  6 COLUMN_ISOLN_REPLY_REQ              
\par  7 EDX_CONFIGURE_REQ                         
\par  8 WDX_CONFIGURE_REQ                        
\par  9 FILAMENT_THRESH_REQ                     
\par A EDX_THRESH_REQ                               
\par B SET_4QBSD_QUADRANT_REQ            
\par C SET_4QBSD_VISIBILITY_REQ            
\par D SET_4QBSD_GAIN_REQ                       
\par E  SET_SCM_RANGE_REQ
\par \pard F  SCM_READINGS_REQUIRED_REQ  
\par 10  VACUUM_TIMER_ROUTINE_REQ
\par 11 WRITE_VACUUM_DATA_REQ     
\par 12 READ_VACUUM_DATA_REQ      
\par 13 OPER_WDX_GATE_VALVE_REQ   
\par 14 AIRLOCK_CONFIGURE_REQ     
\par 15 SET_TILT0                 
\par 16 SET_TOUCH_ALARM_OFF       
\par 17 GET_VACUUM_ERRORS         
\par 18 GET_COMMS_PSU 
\par 19 Specimen Current Monitor measurement error 
\par 
\par The following errors refer to failures in the communications with the Vacuum subsystem
\par 
\par 21 Comms timeout
\par 22 Comms overrun
\par 23 Unknown command
\par \pard 24 Invalid parameter
\par 25 Out of range parameter
\par 26 command failed
\par 27 Bad reply
\par 28 Put Queue error
\par 29 Get Queue error
\par 2A Wrong parameter
\par 2B Space error 
\par 2C Reply parameter error
